<title>USA: Activates EEP to keep US market share - Rep Smith.</title>
<headline>Activates EEP to keep US market share - Rep Smith.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Agriculture Chairman Bob Smith said Monday the United States should &quot;activate&quot; its major export subsidy program to hold on to market share as grain prices fall.</p>
<p>&quot;I want to maintain our market share,&quot; Smith, Oregon-Republican, said during a news conference.</p>
<p>Asked about President Clinton's proposal to allot $500 million in fiscal 1998 for the Export Enhancement Program, Smith said &quot;we ought to activate EEP.&quot;</p>
</text>
